  "query_preview": "../Friday through Monday/...\nA ridge of high pressure lasts over the Gulf and panhandle into \nFriday, however a pattern change begins later Friday into the \nweekend with a return of precipitation as a series of systems move\ninto the area. The first front will move in Friday from a low in \nthe Bering Sea, pushing into the northern Gulf coast Friday night \ninto Saturday morning, as the strong high pressure still looks to \nkeep the front further westward and not fully pushing a front into\nthe rest of the panhandle until Saturday night into Sunday. The \ntiming of this still looks to remain uncertain, largely dependent \non how quickly the high pressure begins to break down and allow \nfor the system to push east into the rest of the panhandle. Even \nmore of the model guidance tonight is keeping the front further \nwest and only pushing in as far as Yakutat through the start of \nSaturday, slowing down the onset of precipitation even further.\n\nAlongside the remaining uncertainty of timing, the precipitation \ntype expected is still uncertain and will depend on the location, \nas some areas may see cold air damming near the surface Saturday \ninto the overnight hours as the front moves in. With this in \nplace, locations at sea level across the northern panhandle may \ninitially see rain with snow mixing in before the warmer \nsubtropical air fully pushes in and makes its way down from the \nupper levels to warm the air near the surface enough to transition\nto rain during the day Sunday.",
